# .chiignore — what Archis does not index. .gitignore syntax.
#
# Your own rules go OUTSIDE the managed block: Archis never touches them.
# Inside the block, Archis appends what it detects as it indexes. Delete an entry from
# inside and Archis takes you at your word: that tree gets indexed, and Archis says so
# once instead of putting the line back.
# To switch a rule off without deleting it, negate it with `!`, e.g. `!dist/`.

# >>> chi: detected <<<
dist/
node_modules/
data/
# <<< chi: end detected >>>
